“He’s been in hospital three times,” put in the Mole;
“and as for the fines he’s had to pay, it’s simply awful to
think of.”

Toad was quite alarmed at this very serious and portentous style of greeting;
but the Rat whispered to him, “Never mind; don’t take any notice;
and don’t say anything to him just yet. He’s always rather low and
despondent when he’s wanting his victuals. In half an hour’s time
he’ll be quite a different animal.”

Presently the Mole came tumbling into the room, evidently very pleased with
himself. “I’ve been having such fun!” he began at once;
“I’ve been getting a rise out of the stoats!”
